settings.liquid:
{%- comment -%}
  Claude Code, 2026-08-27 - pin the hero banner to its right edge.

  The box is a fixed height (375/400/440px) at full-bleed width, so object-fit:
  cover crops the sides, and the theme's default object-position: center splits
  that crop evenly. The subject (glass slide, droplet, caustic) sits at x=1826..3000
  of a 3000px master, so a centred crop cut it in half below ~1900px viewport.
  The left of the master is a deliberately empty extension, so pinning right makes
  every crop fall on flat backdrop instead.

  The tablet band needs a second fix. Between 700 and 1199px the box is 400px tall
  against a narrow width, so cover zooms the master ~1.7x and the caustic moves in
  under the type: measured peak luminance behind the copy goes from 54 to 183 at
  1024px. The text there runs to 81% of the frame (96% at 768px), so there is no
  column left to scrim without dimming the droplet. Cap the text column instead and
  scrim only behind it - the same treatment /pages/the-science uses.

  Scoped with section.id resolved by Liquid at render time, not a hardcoded
  template id - those go stale silently when the template id changes.
{%- endcomment -%}
<style>
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > picture > img,
#shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > img { object-position: right center; }

@media screen and (min-width: 700px) and (max-width: 1199px) {
  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media > div { max-width: min(58vw, 620px); }

  #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .content-over-media::before {
    background-image: linear-gradient(to right, rgba(12,14,18,0.55) 0%, rgba(12,14,18,0.45) 40%, rgba(12,14,18,0.18) 62%, rgba(12,14,18,0) 78%);
  }
}
</style>
